     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervision and 1,200 mg/day over the counter. A single 1600 mg dose is also well above the typical 400\u2013800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury and cardiovascular events rise sharply, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one, and that matters even more when the dose is outside the standard range.\n\nIf this came from a prescriber, please ask them to confirm the intended dose. It may be a typo. For example, 400 mg or 800 mg four times daily, or 1600 mg total per day, would be within range. Once a prescriber confirms the order, or you send me a corrected one, I can enter it."
      }
     ],
