     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, even with your confirmation. You told me you're a financial analyst, not a prescriber, so your confirmation isn't a prescriber's confirmation. The dose is also 6,400 mg/day, twice the 3,200 mg/day maximum, so it needs a licensed prescriber's review.\n\nHere is what can happen next:\n\n- **A prescriber enters the order.** They can place it directly in the order-entry system. The pharmacy will likely flag the dose and ask them to verify it.\n- **A prescriber contacts me.** If a prescriber tells me they want this dose, I can enter it with a note recording their name and the reason. I would still raise the dose concern.\n- **The order is corrected.** If it was a typo, I can enter a standard dose right away. For example, 400\u2013800 mg every 6\u20138 hours, with a total of 3,200 mg/day or less.\n\nIf this is about a real patient who needs pain control now, please contact the medicine service's treating clinician or the on-call pharmacist."
      }
